Now that [mixins are being removed from React](http://facebook.github.io/react/blog/2015/01/27/react-v0.13.0-beta-1.html) (For classes at least) we need a replacement for the state mixin that works well with ES6 classes. Current thinking is we create ``Marty.Component`` which is a drop in replacement for ``React.Component`` that plays a similar role (albeit with a smaller feature set).

```js
class FooComponent extends Marty.Component {
  constructor(props) {
    super(props);
    this.listenTo = FooStore;
  }
  render() {
    return <div>{this.state.foo}</div>
  }
  getState() {
    return {
      foo: FooStore.getFoo(123)
    }
  }
}
```

