comment.body:
Usually I agree with stuff like this, but in this case it just seems so much more trouble... Renaming after `webp()` won't work:

```js
gulp.src('./img/foo.{png,jpg}')
  .pipe(webp())
  .pipe(rename(function (path) {
    console.log(path.extname); // => '.webp';
    // Great... what was the original extension again?
  });
```

While renaming it before doesn't feel right...

```js
gulp.src('./img/foo.{png,jpg}')
  .pipe(rename(function (path) {
    // Add the .webp extension so it can be replaced with the
    // .webp extension... It feels so hacky having to do this.
    path.extname += '.webp';
    // Now I'll have a PNG/JPG stream with a WEBP extension.
  })
  .pipe(webp())
  .pipe(gulp.dest('.'));
```

While, IMHO, when the plugin does that for you, everything just seems to be in the right place. No room for confusion. No time lost. And I don't see it going against the "do one thing and do it well" filosofy, quite the opposite.

If you stick to the `rename()` solution, I believe it would be a good idea to at least add such an example to the docs.

Anyway, thanks for the plugin.

